{"lines":[{"w":0.061804625193278007,"c":1,"t":"Test 1","x":0.088194196541313802,"y":0.050628480993723191,"h":0.013568619359559331},{"t":"recently have been empirically tested in robust ways. Descartes argued that a person only accepts","y":0.097345132963471137,"h":0.016026959939692276,"x":0.086242307050871811,"w":0.83162216186523441,"c":1},{"y":0.11474926280919096,"t":"or rejects information after considering its truth or falsehood; Spinoza argued that people accept","x":0.086242306795856039,"w":0.8234086100260416,"h":0.016064690558959538,"c":1},{"w":0.83367553710937492,"y":0.13067846632098623,"h":0.017699115044247704,"x":0.086242321178371911,"c":1,"t":"all encountered information (or misinformation) by default and then subsequently verify or reject"},{"y":0.15103244810096372,"t":"it through a separate cognitive process. In recent decades, empirical evidence from the research","w":0.8151950581868489,"x":0.086242306532858873,"h":0.014749262536873142,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.086242294206676229,"w":0.82751541137695295,"y":0.16860465127813007,"t":"teams of Erik Asp of the University of Chicago and Daniel Gilbert at Harvard University, among","h":0.016056115929707571},{"c":1,"h":0.017471873865718357,"t":"others, has supported Spinoza's account: people appear to encode all new information as if it","x":0.08624231518200437,"y":0.18459302306395997,"w":0.79466115315755204},{"x":0.088240640187709218,"w":0.81735046386718757,"t":"were true, even if only momentarily, and later tag the information as being either true or false, a","y":0.20130194585040995,"h":0.019807332806882627,"c":1},{"y":0.21953701451570851,"t":"pattern that seems consistent with the observation that mental resources for skepticism physically","h":0.019003703249590886,"x":0.088250243734954104,"c":1,"w":0.82967575073242195},{"t":"reside in a different part of the brain than the resources used in perceiving and encoding.","y":0.23982300912199073,"w":0.75770019531249999,"h":0.015990944246275229,"c":1,"x":0.086242304704544109},{"h":0.014749262536873253,"c":1,"w":0.80287475585937518,"t":"What about our second observation that misinformation often can appear in electronic or print","x":0.090349069604079568,"y":0.27463126834306806},{"h":0.016224188790560423,"y":0.29203539809671231,"x":0.088295700251310338,"t":"media without being preemptively blocked? In support of this, one might consider the nature","w":0.79260777791341153,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"of regulatory structures in the United States: regulatory agencies here tend to focus on post hoc","w":0.81314168294270817,"x":0.086242300087435234,"y":0.30959302327656646,"h":0.017545619615763064},{"c":1,"w":0.79466120402018237,"y":0.32848837220865335,"h":0.016054400441217531,"t":"detection of broadcast information. Organizations such as the Food and Drug Administration","x":0.08624229316170906},{"c":1,"h":0.018945084068275775,"x":0.086242311934521462,"t":"(FDA) offer considerable monitoring and notification functions, but these roles typically do","y":0.34447674468015521,"w":0.78439422607421871},{"w":0.77618067423502612,"x":0.08829569974139323,"t":"not involve preemptive censoring. The FDA oversees direct-to-consumer prescription drug","c":1,"h":0.015988371857499684,"y":0.36337209313872043},{"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1,"y":0.38081395350864877,"w":0.82546203613281255,"x":0.086242287859283243,"t":"advertising, for example, and has developed mechanisms such as the 'Bad Ad' program, through"},{"c":1,"y":0.39970501456386309,"h":0.01599265973476538,"t":"which people can report advertising in apparent violation of FDA guidelines on drug risks.","x":0.08829569974051879,"w":0.77618067423502601},{"w":0.81108830769856777,"x":0.088295681775943727,"h":0.017483878909310691,"t":"Such programs, although laudable and useful, do not keep false advertising off the airwaves. In","y":0.41710914431809198,"c":1},{"x":0.08624231189645741,"t":"addition, even misinformation that is successfully corrected can continue to affect attitudes.","y":0.43451327415977037,"h":0.017521609528578175,"w":0.78439422607421883,"c":1},{"t":"This leads us to our third observation: a campaign to correct misinformation, even if rhetorically","h":0.017699115044247815,"c":1,"w":0.82135523478190109,"x":0.088295688460425764,"y":0.47079645992617503},{"y":0.48837209313874008,"w":0.81108830769856766,"h":0.016052685515367204,"t":"compelling, requires resources and planning to accomplish necessary reach and frequency. For","c":1,"x":0.086242293693670521},{"x":0.086190860574992784,"w":0.80093332926432292,"h":0.020568629352040624,"c":1,"t":"corrective campaigns to be persuasive, audiences need to be able to comprehend them, which","y":0.50399717498363839},{"w":0.77637425740559896,"t":"requires either effort to frame messages in ways that are accessible or effort to educate and","h":0.019248450400203398,"c":1,"x":0.086150765948861854,"y":0.521569541540437},{"h":0.017441860412777621,"w":0.82135523478190098,"t":"sensitize audiences to the possibility of misinformation. That some audiences might be unaware","y":0.54069767427035542,"x":0.086242305894470336,"c":1},{"y":0.55958702056830489,"t":"of the potential for misinformation also suggests the utility of media literacy efforts as early","x":0.086242311911832611,"w":0.78439422607421871,"c":1,"h":0.015994374660615707},{"x":0.086242293455038824,"t":"as elementary school. Even with journalists and scholars pointing to the phenomenon of 'fake","y":0.57699115041347382,"h":0.01603210527988308,"c":1,"w":0.80287475585937496},{"y":0.59439527989001895,"x":0.088295687794282388,"h":0.018976812447066838,"t":"news', people do not distinguish between demonstrably false stories and those based in fact when","c":1,"w":0.8316221618652343},{"w":0.39242851257324218,"h":0.019268062895378191,"c":1,"y":0.61163407720007834,"x":0.086134489826645608,"t":"scanning and processing written information."},{"w":0.82751541137695306,"c":1,"y":0.64825581406870425,"h":0.016050970589516766,"x":0.088295682271410381,"t":"We live at a time when widespread misinformation is common. Yet at this time many people also"},{"w":0.81930185953776036,"x":0.086242293964964467,"y":0.66715116290610832,"h":0.016034677668658626,"c":1,"t":"are passionately developing potential solutions and remedies. The journey forward undoubtedly"},{"h":0.015996947049391363,"c":1,"x":0.088295680734534684,"t":"will be a long and arduous one. Future remedies will require not only continued theoretical","w":0.77823410034179696,"y":0.68459302337141514},{"c":1,"w":0.80903493245442704,"x":0.090349063448757275,"y":0.70203488392828794,"h":0.014534883302221635,"t":"consideration but also the development and maintenance of consistent monitoring tools - and a"},{"y":0.71857575858757738,"x":0.086187903256345635,"h":0.018471487714829316,"t":"recognition among fellow members of society that claims which find prominence in the media","w":0.80709381103515632,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"that are insufficiently based in scientific consensus and social reality should be countered.","y":0.73688364670944606,"w":0.7680514526367187,"h":0.018715723988580901,"x":0.086199634562003483},{"w":0.83162216186523441,"h":0.016050113126591548,"c":1,"t":"Misinformation arises as a result of human fallibility and human information needs. To overcome","y":0.75575221233479006,"x":0.088295695131529517},{"y":0.77315634207918593,"c":1,"t":"the worst effects of the phenomenon, we will need coordinated efforts over time, rather than any","h":0.017541332301136969,"w":0.82340861002604171,"x":0.086242306912315603},{"w":0.43140167236328131,"t":"singular one-time panacea we could hope to offer.","y":0.79003833386631594,"h":0.018946158710130945,"c":1,"x":0.086140885553888796},{"y":0.92441860489760386,"h":0.013081394746943587,"t":"26","x":0.088295688622365934,"w":0.026694043477376306,"c":1},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.45882354736328124,"h":0.04166666666666663,"c":1,"y":0.94166666659226195,"x":0.51176469619230891}],"h":3390,"w":2400}